# K04c (next_core_tasks_v2.md §3 K04, witness matrix row 7; defects.md#sub-actual-number-argument-classification):
# a callable WITHOUT a result is a REFERENCE value, so the canonical nullary call form of one given to a number
# formal is refused as the reference it is -- "a reference where a number is asked", the phrase the Structure
# case already uses (unit_valkind_arg_ref_refused) -- and not as "a callable without a result has no value".
# The atom spelling of the same value is pinned by unit_value_call_sub_refused.
int: y 0

sub: s ()
    y: 3
end: s

fn: g (int: n) int
    return: n
end: g

g(s())
return
